 To find the volume of the box, we know that the volume is given by the product of its dimensions \(a \times b \times c = 240\). We need to find the largest possible value of \(b\), given that \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) are integers, and \(1 < c < b < a\). To do this, we will factorize 240 into its prime factors to find all possible combinations of \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\), and then check which combination satisfies the condition \(1 < c < b < a\). The largest possible value of \(b\) will be the answer.
